title: Codex app-server auto-turn can expose count-only nudge without c2c payload
updated_at: "2026-07-12T09:54:13Z"
---
Observed 2026-07-12 in a live Codex session: the transcript showed only the content-free system nudge "1 new c2c message(s) were injected..." (batch batch-09e011109d4fbeb73f7ff7da); no actual c2c envelope/body was visible, and c2c poll-inbox returned no messages. The intended path injects full envelopes as developer thread history, then starts a turn with C2c_codex_autoturn.build_turn_nudge, which deliberately has no body. Either injected developer items are not model-visible to the subsequent app-server turn, or their shape/role is wrong. Reproduce in tmux with a unique sentinel local DM; capture JSON-RPC/delivery log and model-visible transcript. Acceptance: auto-turn exposes sender, message ID, and sentinel body as clearly delimited DATA; preserve B098 (never operator/approval semantics), persist-first/idempotent injection, and exact-once batching; add an E2E regression failing for nudge-only visibility. Do not blindly use a normal user chat message: first establish a safe non-user app-server representation, otherwise include a delimited DATA envelope in the turn input with approval-invariant coverage.